 "notes": "Combined 95% C.L. BBN + Planck N_eff constraint on the ALP-photon coupling, standard cosmological evolution (blue dashed curve of figure 8 right panel, plots/neff_opt_gphi.pdf in the e-print; same constraint as figure 4 translated from the m-tau to the m-g plane). Curve recovered from the vector paths of the figure PDF (axes m_phi: 1e-2 to 1e3 MeV, g_phigamma: 1e-11 to 1e-3 GeV^-1, both log). The excluded region lies below/left of the curve: for m <~ 2.2 MeV the exclusion extends above the plotted coupling range, so the near-vertical low-mass edge is clamped at the plot top g = 1e-3 GeV^-1; the curve is truncated at the plot edge m = 1 GeV. The paper also shows weakened 'robust' variants allowing extra Delta N_eff and neutrino chemical potential (blue dash-dotted and solid in figure 8); the standard-scenario bound reported here is the paper's main result (section 4). Cosmological bound, no local DM density assumed.",
